    "content": "Kennesaw State University (KSU) is a public university with two main campuses located in suburban Cobb County, Georgia, roughly 15-20 miles northwest of Atlanta. The main campus is in Kennesaw (1000 Chastain Road, Kennesaw, GA 30144), and the second is in Marietta (1100 South Marietta Pkwy, Marietta, GA 30060). Key Campus Locations: Kennesaw Campus: Often referred to as the main campus, located near the historic Kennesaw Mountain National Battlefield Park. Marietta Campus: Formerly Southern Polytechnic State University, this campus is located in Marietta, Georgia, and serves as the home for many engineering and technical programs. Both campuses are within the metro Atlanta area and are easily accessed from major highways like I-75 and I-575.",
